  "description": "HIJVEE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H112 Dy4 N12 O22,6(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.558-3.850 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.48-111.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(μ3-OH)2L6(dbm)4]·6CH3CN (HL = 5-(4-o-hydroxybenzylidene)-8-hydroxylquinoline; dbm = 1,3-diphenyl-1,3-propanedione); C168H130Dy4N18O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
